 "issue": 2470,
 "issue_title": "Bug: schema export accepts or crashes on non-string field names",
 "issue_body": "## Environment / context\n- Repository: `im-anishraj/arnio`\n- Tested against current source on `main` (`78d5ef1e5c7b3af48913a97ae1a02382139532f2`)\n- Python: 3.13.9 in local QA virtualenv\n- Affected APIs: `schema_to_dict`, `schema_to_yaml`\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n```python\nfrom arnio.schema_export import schema_to_dict, schema_to_yaml\n\n# Non-string field names are accepted when every key is the same type.\nschema_to_dict({1: \"int64\"})\nschema_to_yaml({1: \"int64\"})\nschema_to_dict({\"fields\": {1: \"int64\"}})\nschema_to_yaml({\"fields\": {1: \"int64\"}})\n\n# Mixed string/non-string field names fail while sorting, before validation.\nschema_to_dict({\"name\": \"string\", 1: \"int64\"})\nschema_to_yaml({\"name\": \"string\", 1: \"int64\"})\nschema_to_dict({\"fields\": {\"name\": \"string\", 1: \"int64\"}})\nschema_to_yaml({\"fields\": {\"name\": \"string\", 1: \"int64\"}})\n```\n\n## Expected result\nSchema field names should be validated consistently before sorting or emitting output. Non-string field names should either be explicitly rejected with a clear `TypeError` such as `schema field names must be strings`, or intentionally normalized in one documented way.\n\n## Actual result\nCurrent behavior is inconsistent:\n\n```text\nschema_to_dict({1: \"int64\"}) -> {'fields': {1: {'type': 'int64'}}}\nschema_to_yaml({1: \"int64\"}) -> fields:\\n  \"1\":\\n    type: int64\n\nschema_to_dict({\"name\": \"string\", 1: \"int64\"}) -> TypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'int' and 'str'\nschema_to_yaml({\"name\": \"string\", 1: \"int64\"}) -> TypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'int' and 'str'\n```\n\n## Severity / impact\nLow. This is an edge-case validation bug, but schema export is intended to produce deterministic data contracts. Accepting some non-string field keys while crashing on mixed keys can create confusing exports and makes user input validation unpredictable.\n\n## Likely affected area\n- `arnio/schema_export.py::schema_to_dict`\n- `arnio/schema_export.py::schema_to_yaml`\n\n## Suggested next action\nValidate `raw_fields` keys before `sorted(raw_fields.keys())` in both flat and structured schema paths. Add regression tests for all-non-string keys and mixed string/non-string field keys so the error is deliberate and consistent.\n\n## Related but distinct\n- #2395 tracks published wheel parity for path/metadata validation.\n- #2460 tracks mixed scalar set normalization inside field values.\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/2470",
 "pr": 2506,
 "pr_title": "Validate schema export field names before sorting",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\n- validate schema export field names before sorting raw field mappings\n- raise a clear TypeError for non-string field names in flat, structured, and Schema-like inputs\n- add regression coverage for all-non-string and mixed field-name mappings\n\nFixes #2470\n\n## Tests\n- uv run pytest -q tests/test_schema_export.py\n- uv run ruff check .\n- uv run pytest -q\n\n## Notes\n- uv run pyright fails in this environment because pyright is not installed: Failed to spawn: pyright; No such file or directory.\n- uv run ruff format --check . reports pre-existing formatting drift across 32 files unrelated to this change. A focused ruff format diff for arnio/schema_export.py and tests/test_schema_export.py only shows older unrelated lines.",
